\begin{thm}
Let \( \norm{v} \) denote the norm of a vector \( v \). Then, the following properties hold:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \(\norm{v} \geq 0\) for all \( v \), and \(\norm{v} = 0\) if and only if \( v = 0 \).
    \item \(\norm{\alpha v} = |\alpha| \cdot \norm{v}\) for all vectors \( v \) and scalars \( \alpha \).
    \item The triangle inequality: \(\norm{u + v} \leq \norm{u} + \norm{v}\) for all vectors \( u \) and \( v \).
\end{enumerate}
\end{thm}
```

